Skincare Products – Market Research

1. Project Introduction

This project focuses on understanding customer preferences, purchasing behaviour, and expectations regarding skincare products.

2. Project Objectives

- Identify popular skincare products.
- Understand customer buying habits.
- Analyse factors influencing purchasing decisions.
- Understand customer price preferences.
- Identify areas where skincare products can improve.

3. Research Methodology

- Research type: Primary research
- Data collection method: Google Forms
- Total responses: 27
- Target audience: Skincare consumers

4. Key Survey Findings

- 85.2% of respondents use skincare products.
- Face wash was the most selected product.
- 59.3% preferred products priced below ₹200.
- 63% said online reviews influence their buying decisions.
- Product quality was the leading purchase factor.

5. Tools Used

- Google Forms
- Google Sheets
- GitHub

6. Learning Outcomes

Through this project, I learned about:

- Market research and survey creation.
- Customer behaviour analysis.
- Understanding customer preferences.
